  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man in the image",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man (Jussie Smollett) through the textual material's implication that he is the one who 'plays his cards right' to 'skip prison'. The meme frames the man as the subject of the cynical statement, projecting the user's interpretation of his actions and moral character onto him. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me' in the text, but the implied subject of the statement is the man, creating a projection of the user's judgment onto him.",
